      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <z<\\infty .\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of an elliptic cylinder centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is an elliptic cylinder with $a=b=\\sqrt{2}.$",
