    "q-164476": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164476",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-(z-2)^{2}=-1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1,\n$$\n\nand a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1,\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a hyperboloid of two sheets with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(-1,0,2),\\,a=\\sqrt{3},\\,b=2,\\,c=1.\n$$",
