    "q-164512": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164512",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Identify the surface $x=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperbolic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $b=2\\sqrt{2},\\,c=3.$",
